Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:08:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 133/175] feat: retire screen-space sun shafts by default;
 volumetric fog takes over (ReCS cvar defaults)

Three stock cvar DEFAULTS in RendererCVars.cpp, no code path changes:
- r_sunshafts 2 -> 0 (screen-space shafts off; stage, fp16 working set, round-3 bounds and the
  S8 atmospheric condition all remain, r_sunshafts 1 brings them back)
- r_VolumetricFogDownscaledSunShadow 1 -> 2 (third cascade shadowed inside the fog)
- r_VolumetricFogTexScale 10 -> 6 (froxel grid 2.8x finer so fog shafts replace the post effect)
Help strings name the ReCS default and the stock 5.7.1 default. SUNSHAFTS_DEFAULT_VAL in
Renderer.h is left as the stock reference. e_VolumetricFog (Cry3DEngine, restart) unchanged.

Byte identity: the stock path's code is untouched; setting the three stock values back yields the
stock frame. Documented as a ReCS policy exception in ConsoleReference.md (new section), with the
"how to get god rays now" paragraph in SceneReferredContent.md and a retirement note at the head
of SceneReferredCalibration.md section 3.

