+**Screen-space sun shafts are retired (2026-09-09).** `r_sunshafts` now defaults to **0** on
+ReCS; stock CRYENGINE had it at 2. A screen-space shaft is a radial blur of bright pixels with no
+scattering term, no occluder and no path length, and every bound and atmospheric condition the
+scene-referred work bolted onto it was a patch on that approximation. Volumetric fog computes the
+real single-scattering integral, shadow map included, and since S8 it runs on scene units - so it
+is the god-ray source now. To get shafts: `e_VolumetricFog 1` (restart required; put it in the
+project's `system.cfg`), set the Time of Day's volumetric fog `Global density` from the visibility
+table in `SceneReferredCalibration.md` section 3.1 (0.1 = haze, 0.4 = mist; shafts need something
+in the air), and leave `r_VolumetricFogDownscaledSunShadow` (ReCS default 2, stock 1) and
+`r_VolumetricFogTexScale` (ReCS default 6, stock 10) at their ReCS defaults - the first shadows
+the third cascade inside the fog, the second gives the froxel grid 2.8x the resolution. The old
+stage is still in the build: `r_sunshafts 1` brings it back with its scene-referred bounds and
+condition intact, and the calibration in `SceneReferredCalibration.md` section 3 then applies.
+See `ConsoleReference.md`, "Stock engine cvars whose ReCS default differs".
 
